  Generated. It reads the other end's packets and writes the venue's own answers back out. The packets to read are this program's first argument and the file to write is its second, because Emojicode has no standard input. It admits every login: there is nobody for a program like this to ask, so that answer was decided when it was written, which makes it a demonstration of a handshake and never an authenticator.
